1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,031
You've got to fill out your team roster.

2
00:01:53,291 --> 00:01:54,911
Our party organizer needs it.

3
00:01:55,451 --> 00:01:57,331
You each get to participate twice.

4
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,471
And once you've picked your lineup, it's set in stove.

5
00:02:00,831 --> 00:02:02,091
It's got the events listed.

6
00:02:02,711 --> 00:02:05,131
Race, ballgame, and the team contest.

7
00:02:05,451 --> 00:02:06,251
What's that say?

8
00:02:06,491 --> 00:02:09,011
Well, looks like we can all take part in the race.

9
00:02:09,351 --> 00:02:13,151
Three for the ballgame, and then five of us for the team contest.

10
00:02:13,311 --> 00:02:13,731
Cool.

11
00:02:14,291 --> 00:02:16,671
You can go ahead and sign me up for all three.

12
00:02:16,671 --> 00:02:18,071
No, can't do that.

13
00:02:18,311 --> 00:02:19,771
The rules say that two is the limit.

14
00:02:19,771 --> 00:02:22,751
Ugh, we can't lose this thing.

15
00:02:23,031 --> 00:02:25,851
I just know they're going to take Captain Usopp if we do.

16
00:02:26,051 --> 00:02:27,131
No, they aren't.

17
00:02:27,271 --> 00:02:28,571
They're going to take me.

18
00:02:28,771 --> 00:02:29,931
I'm the cute one.

19
00:02:30,291 --> 00:02:35,631
And it's time to announce the rosters each team has chosen to represent them in today's events.

20
00:02:35,891 --> 00:02:38,511
First up, we've got the Straw Hat Pirates.

21
00:02:39,411 --> 00:02:44,011
Participating in round one, the Donut Race, is the entire Straw Hat crew.

22
00:02:44,011 --> 00:02:47,171
Did I ever tell you I got a disease that prevents me from racing?

23
00:02:47,171 --> 00:02:50,451
I don't want to do this stupid race either, so just man up.

24
00:02:51,191 --> 00:02:58,271
Participating in round two, the groggy ring, is Roro Noa Zoro, Sanji, and Tony Tony Chopper.

25
00:02:58,531 --> 00:03:00,231
You better not slow me down.

26
00:03:00,291 --> 00:03:01,351
Right back at you.

27
00:03:01,691 --> 00:03:04,211
I'm going to try my hardest.

28
00:03:04,211 --> 00:03:13,971
And participating in round three, the Run Round Around, we've got Monkey D. Luffy, Nico Robin, Nami, and Usopp.

29
00:03:14,171 --> 00:03:15,651
Aren't we supposed to have five?

30
00:03:16,411 --> 00:03:17,711
We're one member short here.

31
00:03:17,971 --> 00:03:19,251
Well, who cares?

32
00:03:19,351 --> 00:03:20,211
Let's go!

33
00:03:20,211 --> 00:03:25,911
A captain, a swordsman, a navigator, a sniper, a cook, a doctor, and an archaeologist.

34
00:03:26,911 --> 00:03:30,291
So tough, but I do have to decide who it is I'm going to take.

35
00:03:30,891 --> 00:03:32,891
I believe it'd be that one right there.

36
00:03:33,271 --> 00:03:35,051
Yes, that is the one I want.

37
00:03:35,891 --> 00:03:36,771
All right!

38
00:03:36,931 --> 00:03:38,951
Let the merciless Davy back begin!

39
00:03:39,351 --> 00:03:42,951
A winner will be crowned, while the loser will be forcibly drowned.

40
00:03:42,951 --> 00:03:44,751
I am Itaminizu!

41
00:03:45,031 --> 00:03:49,771
You may know me as the Foxy Pirates Party Organizer, but today I will be your commentator!

42
00:03:50,251 --> 00:03:53,911
Our first event of the day is round one, the Donut Race!

43
00:03:54,751 --> 00:03:56,751
How do you guys think we should team up?

44
00:03:56,931 --> 00:03:57,231
Hmm.

45
00:03:58,031 --> 00:04:03,871
Considering that some of us have devil fruit powers, it makes sense to split into two teams of three and four people.

46
00:04:04,011 --> 00:04:08,691
Legal votes for the Donut Race can only be constructed from two oars and three empty barrels.

47
00:04:08,991 --> 00:04:11,751
You will be disqualified if you use any other materials.

48
00:04:11,751 --> 00:04:14,751
This is the perfect chance for shipwrights to show up!

49
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:18,571
If you left your empty barrels at home, come on up here and get some!

50
00:04:18,691 --> 00:04:19,351
All for free!

51
00:04:19,471 --> 00:04:21,351
Because that's how generous we are!

52
00:04:21,531 --> 00:04:26,771
I'm not entirely sure if three barrels is enough material to build a boat big enough to hold all four of us.

53
00:04:26,911 --> 00:04:27,211
Right.

54
00:04:27,471 --> 00:04:29,751
We better go with three teams, insisting of...

55
00:04:31,511 --> 00:04:35,171
What the hell?

56
00:04:35,471 --> 00:04:37,411
You can't just bust them up like that!

57
00:04:37,511 --> 00:04:38,291
Sure I can't!

58
00:04:38,311 --> 00:04:38,971
Just watch!

59
00:04:38,971 --> 00:04:40,891
I am going to make us a killer boat!

60
00:04:41,751 --> 00:04:49,691
All right, I'll take this time while everyone's preparing to explain how the race works.

61
00:04:50,151 --> 00:04:53,911
The course consists of one lap around Long Ring Long Land.

62
00:04:54,291 --> 00:04:57,011
It may sound easy, but believe me, it's not.

63
00:04:57,391 --> 00:05:01,151
If your boat sinks, your team is immediately disqualified from the race.

64
00:05:01,151 --> 00:05:03,391
Oh yeah, weapons, they're allowed!

65
00:05:03,611 --> 00:05:06,491
Guns, cannons, explosives, anything you can think of!

66
00:05:06,711 --> 00:05:10,731
If that sounds unfair, then you've got no right at all to call yourself a pirate!

67
00:05:10,731 --> 00:05:14,011
I'm kind of amazed I've finished.

68
00:05:16,011 --> 00:05:17,951
And time is just about up!

69
00:05:18,111 --> 00:05:19,691
I hope everyone is ready!

70
00:05:21,231 --> 00:05:21,691
Ooh!

71
00:05:22,051 --> 00:05:23,091
Gather round, folks!

72
00:05:23,171 --> 00:05:24,591
The final odds are in!

73
00:05:24,831 --> 00:05:29,151
I'll announce them in order of their popularity, starting with the most popular, of course!

74
00:05:29,531 --> 00:05:30,471
Just as I thought!

75
00:05:30,471 --> 00:05:34,331
The top spot goes to our idle and fellow Foxy Pirate, Porcha!

76
00:05:34,731 --> 00:05:36,551
Oh, you're too kind!

77
00:05:37,091 --> 00:05:39,451
Joining her is the Fishman, Kaputti!

78
00:05:39,791 --> 00:05:43,811
Their vessel is the Cutie Wagon, led by the Star Shark, Mom-Nah!

79
00:05:44,811 --> 00:05:45,331
Yeah!

80
00:05:45,851 --> 00:05:47,071
Take him down, Porcha!

81
00:05:47,151 --> 00:05:48,151
You can do it!

82
00:05:48,611 --> 00:05:49,291
Hold on!

83
00:05:49,371 --> 00:05:51,091
You've got a shark pulling your boat?

84
00:05:51,091 --> 00:05:54,211
I didn't hear him mention any rules forbidding the use of sharks!

85
00:05:54,791 --> 00:05:56,451
The second most popular team?

86
00:05:57,011 --> 00:05:58,691
Well, this is certainly surprising!

87
00:05:59,271 --> 00:06:04,291
It's the Skull Hat team of Navigator Nami, Sniper Usopp, and Archaeologist Robin!

88
00:06:04,731 --> 00:06:06,871
Their official craft is the Barrel Tiger!

89
00:06:07,811 --> 00:06:10,391
That chick with the orange hair is smokin' hot!

90
00:06:10,511 --> 00:06:13,531
I am praying that the dark-haired babe joins our crew!

91
00:06:13,651 --> 00:06:14,651
They can keep the guy!

92
00:06:14,871 --> 00:06:15,671
Yeah, agreed!

93
00:06:16,511 --> 00:06:20,791
Well, sounds like the only thing our Foxy crew cares about are the pretty girls!

94
00:06:20,791 --> 00:06:22,171
What a bunch of hornballs!

95
00:06:23,211 --> 00:06:24,611
You're sure this won't sink?

96
00:06:24,791 --> 00:06:27,791
I told you, I am not a professional shipwright, okay?

97
00:06:28,291 --> 00:06:30,771
But I know it's at least better than those abominations!

98
00:06:31,191 --> 00:06:34,451
Just because it floats doesn't mean it's a boat, it's more like Flotsam!

99
00:06:36,391 --> 00:06:36,831
Flotsam!

100
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:39,031
You've got to do that the whole time?

101
00:06:39,231 --> 00:06:39,531
Yep!

102
00:06:39,751 --> 00:06:41,711
It's a good thing I enjoy riding, huh?

103
00:06:42,091 --> 00:06:43,491
It's a miracle they float!

104
00:06:44,331 --> 00:06:48,051
It's all on our shoulders if our crew's gonna win this race, as usual!

105
00:06:48,051 --> 00:06:50,371
And coming in first on our list is...

106
00:06:50,371 --> 00:06:52,031
The Harem Nocturne!

107
00:06:52,331 --> 00:06:55,811
A beautiful boat full of beautiful women in favor of beautiful people!

108
00:06:56,431 --> 00:06:59,151
In fourth place, we've got the Crab Crane!

109
00:06:59,391 --> 00:07:01,171
An old favorite in the top ranks!

110
00:07:01,471 --> 00:07:05,191
In fifth and sixth place are the Swordfish King 1 and 2!

111
00:07:05,571 --> 00:07:08,271
In seventh place is the Party Love and Pleasure Boat!

112
00:07:08,531 --> 00:07:11,811
And in eighth place, the all-reliable Duke Special!

113
00:07:12,291 --> 00:07:13,151
What's the deal?

114
00:07:13,151 --> 00:07:15,391
You even gonna bother to mention our boat?

115
00:07:15,751 --> 00:07:16,431
Same here!

116
00:07:16,631 --> 00:07:17,291
What gives?

117
00:07:17,631 --> 00:07:18,811
Uh...

118
00:07:18,811 --> 00:07:19,571
Let's see!

119
00:07:19,891 --> 00:07:23,931
Dr. Chopper and Swordsman Zorro's boat, the basically perils is...

120
00:07:23,931 --> 00:07:27,711
Their boat is third to last in popularity!

121
00:07:29,391 --> 00:07:31,671
Yep, I was expecting worse.

122
00:07:31,731 --> 00:07:33,431
And they at least it floats, boat!

123
00:07:34,751 --> 00:07:37,131
Looks like they win the booby prize!

124
00:07:37,811 --> 00:07:39,811
Hey, what's a booby prize?

125
00:07:40,051 --> 00:07:41,991
It means our boat is second to last.

126
00:07:42,671 --> 00:07:45,411
There can't seriously be a boat worse than theirs!

127
00:07:45,591 --> 00:07:47,931
Coming in last on the list of popularity...

128
00:07:47,931 --> 00:07:52,471
We've got the giant barge, the Behemoth Mothership Coaster!

129
00:07:58,411 --> 00:07:59,551
You're kidding me.

130
00:07:59,971 --> 00:08:02,031
The oars can't be long enough for that thing.

131
00:08:02,431 --> 00:08:04,131
How are they supposed to see it?

132
00:08:04,131 --> 00:08:07,271
Yeah, you guys are sharp.

133
00:08:07,771 --> 00:08:09,231
You're right about the oars, though.

134
00:08:09,311 --> 00:08:10,231
Way too short.

135
00:08:10,491 --> 00:08:12,971
And the damn thing is filled with seawater, too!

136
00:08:13,051 --> 00:08:13,771
Not fair!

137
00:08:13,991 --> 00:08:14,751
Those jerks!

138
00:08:14,851 --> 00:08:17,171
Boy, no way that thing is just three barrels.

139
00:08:17,171 --> 00:08:18,211
Sure it is!

140
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:20,831
We pieced together the three biggest barrels we could find.

141
00:08:20,971 --> 00:08:24,051
There ain't nothing in the rule book about how small your barrel's gotta be.

142
00:08:24,551 --> 00:08:27,591
Okay, all of the boats are now at the starting line!

143
00:08:29,771 --> 00:08:34,131
I'll continue to provide commentary throughout the race with a bird's eye view of the action

144
00:08:34,131 --> 00:08:37,171
from atop Chirp Chirp, a rare South Blue Super Sparrow!

145
00:08:37,571 --> 00:08:38,911
Ah, Chirp Chirp!

146
00:08:39,911 --> 00:08:41,751
There you go, what's up?

147
00:08:42,071 --> 00:08:43,771
Yeah, drown that long nose!

148
00:08:43,811 --> 00:08:44,451
Who, me?

149
00:08:44,831 --> 00:08:45,431
That's it!

150
00:08:45,431 --> 00:08:47,071
We have to win this now!

151
00:08:47,171 --> 00:08:48,391
Drowning is fair play.

152
00:08:48,551 --> 00:08:49,291
It's in the rules.

153
00:08:49,711 --> 00:08:51,791
Wow, they think they have a chance of winning!

154
00:08:52,051 --> 00:08:54,491
Let the fools think whatever they want to think, Porcha.

155
00:08:54,691 --> 00:08:56,291
We'll sink them right off the bat.

156
00:08:56,431 --> 00:08:57,251
Right, Monda?

157
00:08:57,631 --> 00:08:58,051
Hey!

158
00:08:58,831 --> 00:09:00,531
I'm excited about this!

159
00:09:00,731 --> 00:09:01,151
What?

160
00:09:01,371 --> 00:09:02,111
About losing?

161
00:09:02,491 --> 00:09:04,071
Now pay close attention, Usopp.

162
00:09:04,211 --> 00:09:07,171
If anything happens to those two ladies, I'll eviscerate you.

163
00:09:07,551 --> 00:09:09,151
We are gonna win this race!

164
00:09:09,171 --> 00:09:09,791
I know it!

165
00:09:09,791 --> 00:09:10,911
Fool!

166
00:09:10,911 --> 00:09:11,911
Fool!

167
00:09:11,911 --> 00:09:14,171
He honestly thinks they're gonna win!

168
00:09:14,171 --> 00:09:15,171
What a riot!

169
00:09:15,171 --> 00:09:17,111
No one's ever beat the Foxy Pirates!

170
00:09:17,111 --> 00:09:19,911
I doubt this race will even last five minutes.

171
00:09:19,911 --> 00:09:20,911
Am I right?

172
00:09:20,911 --> 00:09:21,911
P-p-p-p-p.

173
00:09:21,911 --> 00:09:22,911
You know it.

174
00:09:22,911 --> 00:09:23,291
I know it.

175
00:09:24,291 --> 00:09:29,411
To ensure you don't get lost, we're providing each team with an eternal pose!

176
00:09:30,911 --> 00:09:31,871
Get lost?

177
00:09:33,091 --> 00:09:36,011
Try not to wander too far from the island's coast!

178
00:09:38,631 --> 00:09:40,531
What's this doofus talking about?

179
00:09:40,751 --> 00:09:41,911
Why would we leave the island?

180
00:09:42,371 --> 00:09:44,531
We're taking the inside track the whole way!

181
00:09:44,531 --> 00:09:46,531
I'm afraid it won't be that simple.

182
00:09:46,531 --> 00:09:47,031
What?

183
00:09:47,031 --> 00:09:47,531
Why not?

184
00:09:47,531 --> 00:09:48,531
Take a look.

185
00:09:48,531 --> 00:09:52,731
Excluding the big one in the back, all the other boats are on the outside track facing

186
00:09:52,731 --> 00:09:53,731
out to sea.

187
00:09:53,731 --> 00:09:55,331
It's a little suspicious.

188
00:09:56,531 --> 00:09:57,531
Now!

189
00:09:57,531 --> 00:09:59,531
On your marks!

190
00:10:01,531 --> 00:10:04,031
Get ready!

191
00:10:04,031 --> 00:10:06,031
Just tell me why it won't be simple!

192
00:10:06,031 --> 00:10:07,031
Trust me.

193
00:10:07,031 --> 00:10:08,031
Hey, listen up!

194
00:10:08,031 --> 00:10:11,031
Get away from the shoreline as soon as the race starts!

195
00:10:11,031 --> 00:10:12,031
Huh?

196
00:10:12,031 --> 00:10:13,031
What did he say?

197
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:15,531
Yeah!

198
00:10:15,531 --> 00:10:16,531
Tell me why!

199
00:10:16,531 --> 00:10:17,531
Scheme!

200
00:10:20,531 --> 00:10:22,531
I've got a terrible feeling about this!

201
00:10:22,531 --> 00:10:24,531
No, quit babbling and tell us why already!

202
00:10:24,531 --> 00:10:25,531
Push it!

203
00:10:25,531 --> 00:10:26,531
Push it!

204
00:10:26,531 --> 00:10:27,531
Push it!

205
00:10:27,531 --> 00:10:28,531
Push it!

206
00:10:29,531 --> 00:10:32,531
Time to reveal the secret of our book.

207
00:10:32,531 --> 00:10:34,531
It's got a sneaky little purpose.

208
00:10:41,531 --> 00:10:42,531
Huh?

209
00:10:42,531 --> 00:10:43,531
What's with the barrels?

210
00:10:43,531 --> 00:10:44,531
No!

211
00:10:44,531 --> 00:10:45,531
We didn't get far enough!

212
00:10:45,531 --> 00:10:46,531
What's the big deal?

213
00:10:46,531 --> 00:10:47,531
It's just a barrel.

214
00:10:47,531 --> 00:10:48,531
No, not me!

215
00:10:48,531 --> 00:10:49,531
Don't!

216
00:10:57,531 --> 00:10:58,531
And they've been released!

217
00:10:58,531 --> 00:10:59,531
Look at that!

218
00:10:59,531 --> 00:11:00,531
Kaboom!

219
00:11:00,531 --> 00:11:01,531
The old barrel mines!

220
00:11:01,531 --> 00:11:02,531
The Coaster's Chump Card!

221
00:11:02,531 --> 00:11:03,531
See you later, chumps!

222
00:11:03,531 --> 00:11:06,531
You're supposed to avoid sinking, you know!

223
00:11:06,531 --> 00:11:07,531
Wish us good luck!

224
00:11:07,531 --> 00:11:08,531
Go away!

225
00:11:08,531 --> 00:11:09,531
Dumb bombs!

226
00:11:09,531 --> 00:11:10,531
I'll knock them all back!

227
00:11:10,531 --> 00:11:11,531
Now gum gum!

228
00:11:11,531 --> 00:11:12,531
Cut it out, Luffy!

229
00:11:12,531 --> 00:11:13,531
Stop!

230
00:11:13,531 --> 00:11:15,531
Are you trying to blow us out of the water?

231
00:11:15,531 --> 00:11:16,531
Calm down!

232
00:11:16,531 --> 00:11:17,531
You gotta do something!

233
00:11:17,531 --> 00:11:18,531
Yeah, but that something can't involve touching them!

234
00:11:18,531 --> 00:11:19,531
Luffy, pass that oar over here!

235
00:11:19,531 --> 00:11:20,531
Huh?

236
00:11:20,531 --> 00:11:21,531
What are you doing, Zoro?

237
00:11:21,531 --> 00:11:22,531
Stand back and watch!

238
00:11:22,531 --> 00:11:23,531
Huh?

239
00:11:23,531 --> 00:11:24,531
Huh?

240
00:11:24,531 --> 00:11:25,531
Huh?

241
00:11:25,531 --> 00:11:26,531
What are you doing, Zoro?

242
00:11:26,531 --> 00:11:27,531
Stand back and watch!

243
00:11:27,531 --> 00:11:28,531
Whoa!

244
00:11:28,531 --> 00:11:43,531
They're coming back this way!

245
00:11:43,531 --> 00:11:46,531
It's a mighty hand to the white car!

246
00:11:46,531 --> 00:11:50,531
What am I holding up with the wall right here?

247
00:11:50,531 --> 00:11:56,451
Oh, they're coming back this way!

248
00:12:07,451 --> 00:12:08,731
Oh, crap.

249
00:12:09,471 --> 00:12:10,891
Nami! Robin, look!

250
00:12:11,011 --> 00:12:12,551
Hit the deck and hold on tight!

251
00:12:12,611 --> 00:12:13,931
We gotta ride this wave!

252
00:12:14,891 --> 00:12:17,411
We can't ride this!

253
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:22,531
We can't ride this wave!

254
00:12:34,531 --> 00:12:36,531
Yahoo! This is awesome!

255
00:12:37,531 --> 00:12:39,531
Dammit, she's starting to break up on us!

256
00:12:40,531 --> 00:12:41,531
This is terrifying!

257
00:12:42,531 --> 00:12:43,531
Man, that's cold.

258
00:12:47,531 --> 00:12:48,531
Not good!

259
00:12:50,531 --> 00:12:55,531
I can't believe it!

260
00:12:55,531 --> 00:12:58,531
The Straw Hat team is zipping their way to the front of the race!

261
00:12:58,531 --> 00:12:59,531
This is incredible, folks!

